[SIZE=6][B]MC Macro Mod - Detailed Documentation[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5]► Configuration Breakdown[/SIZE]

The configuration is saved in JSON format under [I].minecraft/config/macromod/config.json[/I]. Below is a detailed description of the parameters you can edit directly or configure via the in-game GUI:

[SIZE=4][B]Default Keybindings & Controls[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Configuration GUI:[/B] Defaults to [B][CODE]`[/CODE][/B] (Grave Accent / Backtick). Opens the full in-game configuration manager.
[*][B]Custom Button Overlay GUI:[/B] Defaults to [B][CODE]M[/CODE][/B]. Opens the transparent, clickable custom button overlay screen.
[*][B]Emergency Kill Switch:[/B] Defaults to [B][CODE]K[/CODE][/B]. Immediately stops all active scripts and releases all held in-game keys (attack, movement, sneak, jump, etc.).
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]1. Event Trigger Parameters[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]durabilityThresholdPercent:[/B] The item durability percentage (0-100) below which the low-durability macro is triggered.
[*][B]lowDurabilityCommand:[/B] The macro string (chat or command) to run when durability is low (e.g. [CODE]/fix all[/CODE]).
[*][B]lowDurabilityActionEnabled:[/B] Toggle to enable/disable the low-durability trigger.
[*][B]healthThresholdPercent:[/B] The health percentage (0-100) below which the low-health macro is triggered.
[*][B]lowHealthCommand:[/B] The macro to run when health is low (e.g. [CODE]/heal[/CODE]).
[*][B]lowHealthActionEnabled:[/B] Toggle to enable/disable the low-health trigger.
[*][B]hungerThresholdLevel:[/B] The food level (0-20 half-hunger points) below which the hunger trigger fires.
[*][B]lowHungerCommand:[/B] The macro to run when food is low.
[*][B]lowHungerActionEnabled:[/B] Toggle to enable/disable the hunger trigger.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]2. Additional Event Triggers[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]inventoryFullActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when the main inventory has no free slots.
[*][B]inventoryFullCommand:[/B] The macro to run on full inventory.
[*][B]joinServerActionEnabled:[/B] If true, runs automatically when joining a server/world.
[*][B]joinServerCommand:[/B] The macro to run upon server join.
[*][B]deathActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when the player dies.
[*][B]deathCommand:[/B] The macro to run upon death.
[*][B]respawnActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when the player respawns after death.
[*][B]respawnCommand:[/B] The macro to run upon respawning.
[*][B]dimensionChangeActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when moving to a new dimension.
[*][B]dimensionChangeCommand:[/B] The macro to run on dimension change.
[*][B]chatTriggerActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when an incoming chat message matches a keyword.
[*][B]chatTriggerFilter:[/B] The keyword/filter string to match in chat messages.
[*][B]chatTriggerCommand:[/B] The macro to run when a chat match occurs.
[*][B]containerOpenActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when opening a container GUI.
[*][B]containerOpenCommand:[/B] Macro to execute on container open.
[*][B]containerCloseActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when closing a container GUI.
[*][B]containerCloseCommand:[/B] Macro to execute on container close.
[*][B]takeDamageActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when taking damage.
[*][B]takeDamageCommand:[/B] Macro to execute when taking damage.
[*][B]lowArmorActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when armor durability falls below threshold %.
[*][B]lowArmorThresholdPercent:[/B] Armor durability % threshold.
[*][B]lowArmorCommand:[/B] Macro to execute on low armor.
[*][B]lowAirActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when remaining air % falls below threshold.
[*][B]lowAirThresholdPercent:[/B] Air/oxygen % threshold.
[*][B]lowAirCommand:[/B] Macro to execute on low air.
[*][B]lowXpActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when XP level falls below threshold.
[*][B]lowXpThresholdLevel:[/B] XP level threshold integer.
[*][B]lowXpCommand:[/B] Macro to execute on low XP level.
[*][B]itemPickupActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when picking up items.
[*][B]itemPickupCommand:[/B] Macro to execute on item pickup.
[*][B]inventoryChangeActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when inventory content changes.
[*][B]inventoryChangeCommand:[/B] Macro to execute on inventory change.
[*][B]worldLoadActionEnabled:[/B] If true, triggers when loading a world or session.
[*][B]worldLoadCommand:[/B] Macro to execute on world load.
[/LIST]

[CENTER]----------------------------------------------------------------[/CENTER]

[SIZE=5]► Scripting Library & Advanced Syntax[/SIZE]

Multi-line scripts are stored as [I].mcm[/I] files under [I].minecraft/config/macromod/scripts/[/I]. The interpreter reads scripts sequentially (one action line per game tick).

[LIST]
[*][CODE]{STASHALL}[/CODE] - Deposits main player inventory items into open container while protecting hotbar pickaxes & shovels.
[*][CODE]{CHAT message}[/CODE] - Sends a chat message or server command with color formatting ([CODE]&a[/CODE] -> [CODE]§a[/CODE]).
[*][CODE]inc var [step][/CODE] / [CODE]dec var [step][/CODE] - Increments or decrements variable by step amount.
[*][CODE]add var val[/CODE], [CODE]sub var val[/CODE], [CODE]mul var val[/CODE], [CODE]div var val[/CODE], [CODE]mod var val[/CODE] - Native arithmetic operations.
[*][CODE]concat(target, s1, s2)[/CODE], [CODE]substr(var, start, len)[/CODE], [CODE]length(target, var)[/CODE] - String manipulation.
[*][CODE]lower(var)[/CODE], [CODE]upper(var)[/CODE] - Case conversion.
[*][CODE]arraypush(arr, val)[/CODE], [CODE]arraypop(arr, [target])[/CODE], [CODE]arrayclear(arr)[/CODE], [CODE]arraycontains(arr, val, target)[/CODE] - Array operations.
[*][CODE]{READFILE "file.txt" arrayVar}[/CODE] - Reads file lines into a named array variable.
[*][CODE]{ARRAYSIZE arrayVar targetVar}[/CODE] - Stores array length into a target variable.
[*][CODE]{GETARRAY arrayVar index targetVar}[/CODE] - Retrieves element by index into target variable.
[*][CODE]{INVENTORYGETSLOT item_id varName}[/CODE] - Returns slot index holding item.
[*][CODE]{GETHELDITEM varName}[/CODE] - Stores main-hand item name into variable.
[*][CODE]{GETCONTAINERTITLE varName}[/CODE] - Stores open screen title into variable.
[*][CODE]{SWAPSLOT from to}[/CODE] - Swaps two inventory slot positions.
[*][CODE]{WAITUNTIL condition [timeout_ticks]}[/CODE] - Non-blocking wait until condition is true or optional timeout elapses.
[*][CODE]{LOOKRANGE 87 93 -3 3}[/CODE] - Looks at a random spot within explicit min/max boundaries ([I]minYaw maxYaw minPitch maxPitch[/I]).
[*][CODE]{LOOKRANDOM 90 0 3 3}[/CODE] (or [CODE]{LOOKVARIANCE}[/CODE]) - Looks at a random spot centered at ([I]90, 0[/I]) with ±3° yaw & pitch variance ([I]centerYaw centerPitch yawSpread pitchSpread[/I]).
[*][CODE]{LOOKAT x y z [expectedBlock] [innerMargin]}[/CODE] - Smoothly rotates player camera using human WindMouse curves to face target coordinates ([I]x, y, z[/I]). Supports optional block validation (e.g. [I]furnace[/I], [I]blast_furnace[/I]) and inner margin depth ratio ([I]0.0[/I] to [I]0.45[/I]).
[*][CODE]{VERIFYSCREEN interfaceName}[/CODE] - Verifies that active screen title or class matches [I]interfaceName[/I] (e.g. [I]furnace[/I], [I]chest[/I], [I]vault[/I]). Halts script if mismatched.
[*][CODE]{WAIT 20 50}[/CODE] or [CODE]{WAITRANDOM 20 50}[/CODE] - Waits a random duration between 20 and 50 ticks.
[*][CODE]$random[/CODE] / [CODE]$rand[/CODE] - Built-in variable returning a random float between 0.0 and 1.0.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]Read-Only Player & World State Variables[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][CODE]$isburning[/CODE], [CODE]$onfire[/CODE], [CODE]$isswimming[/CODE], [CODE]$eyeheight[/CODE] - Burn state, swimming state, and player eye height.
[*][CODE]$xpos[/CODE], [CODE]$ypos[/CODE], [CODE]$zpos[/CODE] - Player's current coordinates.
[*][CODE]$health[/CODE], [CODE]$maxhealth[/CODE] - Player's health stats.
[*][CODE]$hunger[/CODE] - Player's food level (0-20).
[*][CODE]$invfull[/CODE], [CODE]$isfurnaceopen[/CODE], [CODE]$ischestopen[/CODE], [CODE]$iscraftingopen[/CODE], [CODE]$isanvilopen[/CODE] - Returns 1 if inventory or specific interface is open, 0 otherwise.
[*][CODE]$screentitle[/CODE], [CODE]$screenclass[/CODE], [CODE]$containertype[/CODE] - Exact text title, class name, and menu type of active GUI screen.
[*][CODE]$speed[/CODE] - Player's current speed.
[*][CODE]$durability[/CODE] - Held item durability percentage (0-100).
[*][CODE]$offhanddurability[/CODE], [CODE]$helmetdurability[/CODE], [CODE]$chestdurability[/CODE], [CODE]$leggingsdurability[/CODE], [CODE]$bootsdurability[/CODE] - Armor/offhand durability percentages.
[*][CODE]$targetname[/CODE], [CODE]$targethealth[/CODE], [CODE]$targetmaxhealth[/CODE] - Targeted block or mob name & health.
[*][CODE]$iteminhand[/CODE], [CODE]$freeinventory[/CODE] - Name of held item and number of free inventory slots.
[*][CODE]$israining[/CODE], [CODE]$isnight[/CODE], [CODE]$blockbelow[/CODE] - Weather boolean, night boolean, and block underneath player.
[*][CODE]$biome[/CODE], [CODE]$dimension[/CODE], [CODE]$server[/CODE] - Current biome, dimension, and server IP.
[*][CODE]$fps[/CODE], [CODE]$ping[/CODE], [CODE]$time[/CODE], [CODE]$light[/CODE] - Frames per second, latency, world time, and light level.
[*][CODE]$yaw[/CODE], [CODE]$pitch[/CODE], [CODE]$slot[/CODE], [CODE]$mainhand[/CODE], [CODE]$offhand[/CODE] - Orientation, hotbar slot index, main hand item name, and off hand item name.
[*][CODE]$level[/CODE], [CODE]$xp[/CODE], [CODE]$xpprogress[/CODE], [CODE]$xppercent[/CODE] - Player experience level and level progress %.
[*][CODE]$air[/CODE], [CODE]$oxygen[/CODE], [CODE]$maxair[/CODE] - Remaining air supply and max air supply.
[*][CODE]$saturation[/CODE], [CODE]$armor[/CODE] - Food saturation level and total armor protection points.
[*][CODE]$facing[/CODE], [CODE]$direction[/CODE], [CODE]$gamemode[/CODE], [CODE]$difficulty[/CODE], [CODE]$weather[/CODE] - Direction facing, gamemode, difficulty, and weather string.
[*][CODE]$isthundering[/CODE], [CODE]$underwater[/CODE], [CODE]$onground[/CODE], [CODE]$isriding[/CODE], [CODE]$issneaking[/CODE], [CODE]$issprinting[/CODE], [CODE]$isflying[/CODE] - Player and world state booleans (1 or 0).
[*][CODE]$playername[/CODE], [CODE]$username[/CODE] - Player username string.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]Control Flow[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]While Loops:[/B]
[CODE]
while $health > 10
    # Loop body
endwhile
[/CODE]
[*][B]If/Else Conditionals:[/B]
[CODE]
if $durability < 20
    /say Durability critical!
else
    /say All good!
endif
[/CODE]
[*][B]Helper Commands:[/B]
[LIST]
[*][CODE]stop[/CODE] - Stops the current script immediately.
[*][CODE]stopall[/CODE] - Stops all running scripts immediately.
[*][CODE]call <script_name>[/CODE] - Runs a separate script file asynchronously.
[/LIST]
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]LuckPerms Integration & Server Meta-Keys[/B][/SIZE]
Server admins running the [CODE]macromod-server[/CODE] companion plugin with LuckPerms installed can set granular per-group or per-player permission overrides using standard LuckPerms meta commands:
[LIST]
[*][CODE]/lp group default meta set macromod.allowMovement false[/CODE] - Disables movement automation macros for default group.
[*][CODE]/lp group vip meta set macromod.allowScriptFiles true[/CODE] - Enables script files for VIP group.
[*][CODE]/lp user <player> meta set macromod.chatRateLimitMs 2000[/CODE] - Sets a 2000ms chat rate limit for a specific player.
[*][B]Supported Meta Flags:[/B] [CODE]macromod.allowMovement[/CODE], [CODE]macromod.allowLook[/CODE], [CODE]macromod.allowInventoryAutomation[/CODE], [CODE]macromod.allowScriptFiles[/CODE], [CODE]macromod.allowLooping[/CODE], [CODE]macromod.maxLoopIterations[/CODE], [CODE]macromod.chatRateLimitMs[/CODE], [CODE]macromod.commandRateLimitMs[/CODE], [CODE]macromod.allowEventTriggers[/CODE].
[/LIST]

[CENTER]----------------------------------------------------------------[/CENTER]

[SIZE=5]► Key Combinations & Keycodes[/SIZE]

Key IDs follow the GLFW keycode standard. 
Modifiers are represented by adding a bitmask prefix:
[LIST]
[*][B]Shift:[/B] Adds 1
[*][B]Ctrl:[/B] Adds 2
[*][B]Alt:[/B] Adds 4
[/LIST]
For example, pressing [B]Ctrl + Space[/B] (GLFW Key 32) creates the key identifier: [CODE]KEY_32_MOD_2[/CODE].
You can find a complete listing of keycodes in the [I]KEYCODE.md[/I] file in the mod folder.

